UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Moimoi with Pap combines the classic Nigerian steamed bean pudding with fermented corn porridge. Moimoi, made from blended black-eyed peas, is a protein-rich Nigerian staple served at celebrations. Paired with pap (ogi), this combination represents the balanced nutrition of traditional Yoruba cuisine.' WHERE slug = 'moimoi-pap-ng';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Moin Moin (Steamed Bean Pudding) is a beloved Nigerian dish made from ground black-eyed peas steamed with peppers, onions, and spices. This nutritious pudding represents the ingenious West African tradition of transforming legumes into diverse preparations. It''s a celebration staple across Nigeria.' WHERE slug = 'moi-moi-ng';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Ofada Rice with Ayamase Sauce is a Yoruba specialty featuring locally grown ofada rice with a green pepper sauce. The unpolished ofada rice, named after the town in Ogun State, represents Nigeria''s indigenous rice cultivation traditions. Ayamase''s intense green pepper flavor is uniquely Nigerian.' WHERE slug = 'ofada-rice-ng';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Ogbono Soup is made from ground ogbono (African bush mango) seeds, prized for their mucilaginous texture. This traditional Nigerian soup, popular among the Igbo and Yoruba, represents the deep knowledge of indigenous plant-based cooking in West Africa. The draw (slimy) texture is considered a delicacy.' WHERE slug = 'ogbono-soup-ng';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Okra Soup is one of Nigeria''s most popular soups, cherished for its nutritious, mucilaginous qualities. Okra has been cultivated in West Africa for millennia and is central to countless dishes. This versatile soup pairs with various swallows and represents everyday Nigerian home cooking.' WHERE slug = 'okra-soup-ng';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Suya Skewers represent Nigeria''s most famous street food tradition from the Hausa people. The yaji spice blend of ground peanuts, ginger, and cayenne creates suya''s distinctive flavor. Sold at roadside spots across Nigeria, suya brings communities together in the evening social ritual.' WHERE slug = 'suya-skewers-ng';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Abacha (African Salad) from Nigeria is a unique dish of dried cassava flakes mixed with palm oil, ugba, and garden eggs. This Igbo specialty is a centerpiece at Eastern Nigerian celebrations and represents the sophisticated fermentation and preservation techniques of the Igbo culinary tradition.' WHERE slug = 'abacha-african-salad-nigeria';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Ayamase (Ofada Green Stew) is a fiery green pepper sauce from Yoruba cuisine, traditionally served with local ofada rice. This complex stew uses green bell peppers, scotch bonnet peppers, and locust beans (iru) to create deep, layered flavors unique to southwestern Nigerian cooking.' WHERE slug = 'ayamase-ofada-green-stew-nigeria';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Egusi Soup is arguably Nigeria''s most iconic soup, made from ground melon seeds with leafy vegetables and assorted proteins. Egusi seeds have been a cornerstone of West African nutrition for thousands of years, providing essential fats and protein in a rich, flavorful preparation.' WHERE slug = 'egusi-soup-nigeria';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Ewa Agoyin is a Yoruba street food of mashed beans served with a fiery palm oil sauce. Named after the Togolese and Beninese (Agoyin) migrants who popularized it in Lagos, this dish represents the culinary cross-pollination within West Africa and the vibrant street food culture of Lagos.' WHERE slug = 'ewa-agoyin';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Kilishi is Nigerian spiced jerky from the Hausa people, air-dried and coated with a paste of groundnuts and spices. This ancient preservation technique has sustained travelers and traders across the Sahel for centuries. Kilishi represents the sophisticated meat preservation traditions of Northern Nigeria.' WHERE slug = 'kilishi-spiced-jerky';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Ofe Nsala (White Soup) is an Igbo delicacy from southeastern Nigeria, made without palm oil to create a clear, flavorful broth. Often served with catfish and pounded yam, it represents the refined culinary traditions of the Igbo people and is a must-have at important celebrations and ceremonies.' WHERE slug = 'ofe-nsala-white-soup-nigeria';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Ofe Oha (Oha Leaf Soup) is a traditional Igbo soup made with the aromatic oha (ora) leaves unique to southeastern Nigeria. This nutritious soup, thickened with cocoyam, represents the deep botanical knowledge of Igbo cuisine and the important role of indigenous leafy vegetables in West African cooking.' WHERE slug = 'ofe-oha-leaf-soup-nigeria';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Puff-Puff are beloved West African fried doughnuts, sweet and airy balls of yeast-risen dough. In Nigeria, puff-puff is essential at every celebration and sold by street vendors nationwide. This simple yet irresistible treat represents the joy of communal eating and festive Nigerian food culture.' WHERE slug = 'puff-puff-african-doughnuts';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Suya is Nigeria''s most iconic street food, spiced grilled meat skewers from the Hausa people. The yaji spice blend creates suya''s unmistakable flavor. Evening suya spots are social institutions across West Africa, bringing together people from all walks of life around the grill.' WHERE slug = 'suya-nigeria';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Yam Pottage (Asaro) is a hearty Yoruba one-pot dish of yam chunks cooked in a spiced tomato and pepper sauce. Yam is sacred in Yoruba culture, with the New Yam Festival (Iwa Ji) celebrating the annual harvest. This comfort food represents the deep cultural significance of yam in Nigeria.' WHERE slug = 'yam-pottage';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Masa (Waina) are traditional Hausa rice cakes from Northern Nigeria, fermented and fried in special round molds. This street food staple represents the sophisticated grain preparation techniques of the Hausa people, who have cultivated rice and millet for generations across the Sahel.' WHERE slug = 'masa-waina-nigeria-north';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Miyan Geda (Groundnut Soup) is a creamy peanut soup from Northern Nigeria, central to Hausa cuisine. Groundnuts are the backbone of Northern Nigerian agriculture, and this protein-rich soup, served with tuwo (pounded rice or grain), represents the Hausa people''s masterful use of indigenous ingredients.' WHERE slug = 'miyan-geda-groundnut-soup-nigeria-north';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Miyan Kuka (Baobab Leaf Soup) features the leaves of the iconic African baobab tree, a superfood that has sustained Sahelian communities for millennia. This nutritious, slightly sour soup from Northern Nigeria represents the ancient tradition of using every part of Africa''s most sacred tree.' WHERE slug = 'miyan-kuka-baobab-soup-nigeria';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Tuwo Shinkafa with Miyan Taushe is a Northern Nigerian staple pairing soft rice dough with pumpkin-based soup. This combination represents the agricultural traditions of the Nigerian savanna where rice and pumpkin cultivation have sustained communities for centuries.' WHERE slug = 'tuwo-shinkafa-miyan-taushe-nigeria';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Eru (Afang) Soup is a popular vegetable soup from the Cross River and Cameroon regions, made with wild-foraged eru leaves (okongobang). This cross-border dish represents the shared culinary heritage of the Nigeria-Cameroon borderlands and the tradition of harvesting wild forest greens.' WHERE slug = 'eru-afang-soup-nigeria-cameroon';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Global', history = 'Egusi Ramen fusion combines Nigerian egusi soup with Japanese ramen, representing the creative cross-cultural culinary innovation of the African diaspora. This fusion dish emerged from Nigerian-Japanese food enthusiasts and showcases how West African flavors can transform global comfort foods.' WHERE slug = 'egusi-ramen-fusion';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Global', history = 'Suya Spiced Noodles blend Nigeria''s iconic yaji suya spice with Japanese noodle traditions. This fusion dish represents the growing global appreciation for West African flavors and their creative application in new culinary contexts. It''s a testament to the universality of Nigeria''s spice culture.' WHERE slug = 'suya-spiced-noodles';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Fura da Nono is a traditional Hausa-Fulani refreshing drink of fermented millet balls served in fresh cow''s milk. This nutritious beverage has sustained pastoral Fulani communities across Nigeria and Niger for centuries, representing the nomadic dairy traditions of West Africa''s Sahelian peoples.' WHERE slug = 'fura-da-nono-nigeria-niger';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Oceania', history = 'Pavlova is a meringue-based dessert with whipped cream and fresh fruit, claimed by both Australia and New Zealand. Named after Russian ballerina Anna Pavlova during her 1920s tours, this light, crispy-outside-soft-inside dessert has become the quintessential Antipodean celebration cake.' WHERE slug = 'pavlova-nz';
